  book_summary: Little Red Riding Hood is a beloved little girl, especially cherished by her grandmother, who gives her a red velvet cap and from then on she is known by that name. Her mother sends her through the forest with cake and wine to visit her sick grandmother. Along the way, she meets a wolf who asks where she is going. The wolf then goes straight to the grandmother’s house, knocks, and pretends to be Little Red Riding Hood bringing cake and wine. Too weak to get up, the grandmother tells him to press the latch, and when he does, he enters, goes to her bed, and devours her.


